1:["$","main",null,{"className":"task-page","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"site-header","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"chrome-inner","children":[["$","a",null,{"className":"header-name","href":"/","aria-current":"$undefined","children":"AI Infra Bench"}],["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Primary navigation","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/leaderboard.html","aria-current":"$undefined","children":"Leaderboard"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/tasks.html","aria-current":"page","children":"Tasks"}],["$","a",null,{"className":"github-link","href":"https://github.com/ai-infra-bench/ai-infra-bench","children":"GitHub"}]]}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"task-detail","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"task-detail-heading","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"Runner V2 Selection"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Enable automatic Model Runner V2 selection for supported Qwen3 models while honoring explicit overrides."}]]}],["$","$La",null,{"instructionHtml":"<p>Let vLLM choose the model runner when <code>VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER</code> is unset. For this initial rollout, default to V2 only for supported dense, unquantized Qwen3 text-generation configurations. Leave other configurations on V1.</p>\n<p>Keep the explicit overrides: <code>0</code> forces V1, and <code>1</code> requests V2, including compatible models outside the automatic rollout. Base the choice on what the current V2 runner supports. In auto mode, leave unsupported configurations on V1; if <code>1</code> is explicitly set, fail startup with a clear error. There’s no need to add support for new features in V2.</p>\n<p>Make sure the engine worker actually starts with the selected runner, rather than making a conflicting choice from the environment default.</p>","verifierFiles":[{"name":"test.sh","lineCount":29,"url":"/generated/task-files/vllm-runner-v2-selection/tests/0.json"},{"name":"checkpoint.c","lineCount":93,"url":"/generated/task-files/vllm-runner-v2-selection/tests/1.jso